Z||000014||Guinea Pig||02-09-2000||04:10 AM||||I believe there was a picture in a recent article in one of the Kit Car mags or High Performance Pontiac showing a Fiero with the Trans Am front fender air extracters used as hood vents.  The article was by Joe Wynmann of Associated Auto.  The article was about the longitudinal installation of an SBC in the Fiero.<BR>Oreif, is that the hood vent that V-8 Archie makes?  Is he now producing them for sale?  The last I spoke with him he didn't indicate he was going to do that.<BR>The FOCOA lists the snorkle style scoop in their catalog.  At least they did before the "re-organization". ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Monkeyman||02-09-2000||07:27 AM||||IRM has the Indy style scoop advertised in their catalog.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Oreif||02-09-2000||09:07 AM||||Monkeyman is correct, I got mine from IRM. The scoop is originally designed for the '84 Fiero. You have to trim the bottom to fit '85 thru '88 (including fastback GT). When you get the scoop it has markings on it as to '85 - '88 notchback (the hump angle) and fastback GT (decklid is higher). The trimming instructions are very clear. ||||reg||1
